# Make a Dragonkin, let him grow Hungry, photograph him, let him grow
# Starving, photograph him again.
#
# ONE ASSERTION, bd inc-i9q.3: getting hungrier must never make a character
# stronger. The sidebar prints STR and CON (src/Term.cpp), and those two
# numbers must not go UP between the two photographs.
#
# Keep the original Dragonkin barbarian: Burning Hunger rank 3 multiplies
# the new per-turn clock by three (inc-i9q.2).
#
# THE COUNTS. Starting hunger is 2890. A Search advances about 1500 ticks,
# costing roughly 4 points at rank 3 after the Spd 70% multiplier
# (3 * 0.85 * 1500 / 1008), not the old 100. Searches shorten as hunger grows.
# Sixty Searches reach Hungry (1001..2750); 440 more reach Starving
# (501..1000). Seed 1 and options-2026-08-22.dat pin the random drain.
# The state assertions and the unchanged check verify all three photographs.
#
# Race, subrace, class and alignment use @choose by name, so changing a
# list cannot shift these selections. Run with a fixed seed;
# tools/check_hunger_penalty.sh supplies one. Attribute sets have no names,
# and the rolls decide which feats are offered, so those picks stay counted.
# Start-menu, yes/no and movement keys stay positional for the reasons below.

@expect "Initial Choices"
a       # Create a New Character: start menu is not a screen @choose reads.
@expect "Alter the character generation options?"
n       # No alteration: a yes/no question, not a menu.
@expect "Explore Mode. Continue?"
y       # Continue in Explore Mode: a yes/no question, not a menu.
@choose "Lizardfolk"
@choose "Dragonkin"
@choose "Barbarian"
@expect "Which of the five attribute sets"
a       # First attribute set: the five offered sets have no names.
@choose "Neutral"
@expect "Choose a feat"
a       # First feat: the offered feats depend on attribute rolls.
@expect "Choose a feat"
a       # Second feat: the offered feats depend on attribute rolls.

# Skill Manager. Three RIGHTs per skill spends everything available
# without needing to know how many ranks this character has.
# The old comment said Skill Manager twice; corrected 2026-09-12.
@expect "Skill Manager"
# Cursor movement, not a choice.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
# Finish ranks, then confirm: ENTER is a control; y answers yes/no.
ENTER y

@expect "Your personality archetype"
y       # No match: the sixteen personality entries use [a] through [p].
# The old comment called this worship; corrected 2026-09-12.
# RIGHT/DOWN move the personality selection to The Manipulative Plotter.
# Personality affects only the sheet banner, so its selection is not pinned.

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
# Accept the personality, then dismiss the Entry Chamber description.
ENTER y

# In the dungeon now, and Satiated. This first photograph is the baseline: it
# carries no hunger penalty at all, and it is what says the two below have
# moved.
@expect "Satiated"
@dump:fed

s*60    # Search, sixty times
@expect "Hungry"
@dump:hungry

s*440   # 440 more Searches (500 total)
@expect "Starving"
@dump:starving

@quit
